If a patient agrees to a lower-opioid-dosage-taper then every clinician should establish a continued-opioid-goal with the patient.
If a patient agrees to a lower-opioid-dosage-taper and a nonpharmacologic-treatment is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonpharmacologic-treatment.
If a patient agrees to a lower-opioid-dosage-taper and a nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment.
If a patient continues a high-dosage-opioid then every clinician should establish a continued-opioid-goal with the patient.
If a patient continues a high-dosage-opioid and a nonpharmacologic-treatment is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonpharmacologic-treatment.
If a patient continues a high-dosage-opioid and a nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment is appropriate for the patient then every clinician should maximize the nonopioid-pharmacologic-treatment.
